<title>UK: Libya keeps Sept crude prices steady from Aug.</title>
<headline>Libya keeps Sept crude prices steady from Aug.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Libya told contract customers on Monday it was rolling over its crude oil contract prices from August into September, a National Oil Company (NOC) official said.  </p>
<p>As a result, the price of Libya's key export grade Es Sider has been kept unchanged at 15 cents a barrel under Dated Brent.</p>
<p>The NOC official said the price freeze took into consideration the current market conditions for Libyan crude and similar grades in the Mediterranean.</p>
<p>Table of Libyan crude contract prices in dollars per barrel:  </p>
<p> CRUDE			    SEPT	 AUG</p>
<p> Amna	   Dated Brent  -$0.55    -$0.55</p>
<p> Brega	  Dated Brent  +$0.30    +$0.30</p>
<p> Bouri	  Iran Heavy   -$0.35    -$0.35</p>
<p> Es Sider     Dated Brent  -$0.15    -$0.15</p>
<p> Sarir	  Dated Brent  -$0.50    -$0.50</p>
<p> Sirtica	Dated Brent  -$0.10    -$0.10</p>
<p> Zuetina	Dated Brent  +$0.30    +$0.30</p>
<p>--Karen Matusic, London newsroom, +44 171 542 6280</p>
